        'Present: Played in Finland as part of the Jass tradition',
      ],
      evolution: 'The game evolved from Swiss Jass through German and Austrian intermediaries, adapting to Finnish card game preferences. The kontra (doubling) mechanism became a defining feature, allowing opponents to challenge the declaring side.',
      cultural: 'Jass games are popular across Northern and Central Europe. In Finland, Kontra represents the local expression of this tradition, played in social and family settings.',
